      "writtenOn": "2026-11-24T06:01:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This lets anyone with `Create Project` write any per-repo Git config, which until now only admins with filesystem access could do. Like, `uploadpack.allowAnySHA1InWant \u003d true` makes JGit\u0027s UploadPack accept any want, which gets around Gerrit\u0027s ref visibility filtering for that repo. `include.path` makes JGit read an arbitrary server file on every open. Should `git_config` require `Administrate Server` (or `Maintain Server`), or be limited to an allowlist of keys?",
      "revId": "7d80e573c3ba27d5f96af6e19daf4c62f1283222",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
